---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const projects = (await getCollection('projects', ({ data }) => !data.draft)).sort(
  (a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf()
);
---

<Base title="GregBenza.ai — where good ideas go to grow">
  <h1>About Me</h1>
  <p>
    GregBenza.AI is a public proof-of-work: a living blog that shows what Greg actually
    builds — not what he claims. In a world where anyone can write the perfect résumé,
    showing your work is the only credential left.
  </p>
  <p>
    The projects and the methods behind them, released on the rhythm a release scheduler
    sets from what the backlog holds — until the site catches up to the present, then
    keeps pace with it from there. Showing is the floor.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site transfers: every post carries depth underneath — the files, skills, and
    workflows behind the work, packaged so a visitor walks out with something they can
    run today — and connects one click into the visitor's own AI, prompts preloaded, so
    interrogating the work is one click deep. The door swings both ways: visitors talk
    back, poke holes, and say what to build differently, and the work gets better for it.
    A conversation, not a monument.
  </p>
  <p>
    Built agent-first for the AI that visits — when someone asks their AI "who's doing
    interesting work," this site is what it finds and quotes — with research-grade UX for
    the human it reports to. The machinery is AI-run: Claude sessions read the projects,
    draft the updates, publish on Greg's approval, and earn autonomy one proven rung at a
    time. The site running itself is part of the exhibit.
  </p>

  <hr />

  <p class="eyebrow">The log</p>
  {
    projects.length === 0 ? (
      <p>Nothing here yet — the census fills this in.</p>
    ) : (
      <ul class="project-list">
        {projects.map((p) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`/projects/${p.id}/`}>
              <span class="title">{p.data.title}</span>
              <span class="blurb">{p.data.blurb}</span>
              <time datetime={p.data.date.toISOString()}>
                {p.data.date.toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' })}
              </time>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    )
  }
</Base>

<style>
  .project-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .project-list li {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .project-list a {
    display: block;
    padding: var(--space-3) 0;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .project-list .title {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  .project-list .blurb {
    display: block;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin-top: var(--space-1);
  }
  .project-list time {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    margin-top: var(--space-1);
  }
</style>
